go-in-lean contains material derived from source code of the Go programming
language (https://go.dev):

- Lean 4 transliterations of, and lookup tables generated from, src/math/bits
  (bits.go, bits_tables.go), src/slices and src/sort of release go1.25.5;
- Lean theorems generated from the SSA rewrite rules of
  src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/_gen/generic.rules (go1.25.5, and master for
  the rules checked by check_new_rules), of ARM64.rules and AMD64.rules (the
  revision is recorded by sha256 in each generated file), and from the
  magic-constant division of src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/magic.go;
- patches against the Go source tree (findings/*/fix.patch and the change
  packages in findings/*/cl/), and Go source quoted in the finding write-ups.

